<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/1037642>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Although the mentioned detection method is theoretically possible, the use of speculative execution is a preferred way of increasing processor performance. The reality is that a large number of statements are executed out of order, and determining if any of them break an access control property would be extremely opportunistic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/116381>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"This is not a perfect solution, since 100% accuracy and coverage are not feasible." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/119860>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Detection techniques for buffer-related errors are more mature than for most other weakness types." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/120860>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Detection techniques for buffer-related errors are more mature than for most other weakness types." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/129846>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"This is not a perfect solution, since 100% accuracy and coverage are not feasible." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/131636>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Without visibility into the code, black box methods may not be able to sufficiently distinguish this weakness from others, requiring follow-up manual methods to diagnose the underlying problem." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/131775>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"These may be more effective than strictly automated techniques. This is especially the case with weaknesses that are related to design and business rules." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/131868>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Detection techniques for buffer-related errors are more mature than for most other weakness types." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/190642>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Without visibility into the code, black box methods may not be able to sufficiently distinguish this weakness from others, requiring follow-up manual methods to diagnose the underlying problem." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/190775>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"These may be more effective than strictly automated techniques. This is especially the case with weaknesses that are related to design and business rules." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/2501290>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Note that this technique is only useful for privilege issues related to system resources. It is not likely to detect application-level business rules that are related to privileges, such as if a blog system allows a user to delete a blog entry without first checking that the user has administrator privileges." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/250454>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"These may be more effective than strictly automated techniques. This is especially the case with weaknesses that are related to design and business rules." .
