<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/7321281>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Note that this technique is only useful for permissions issues related to system resources. It is not likely to detect application-level business rules that are related to permissions, such as if a user of a blog system marks a post as \"private,\" but the blog system inadvertently marks it as \"public.\"" .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/732454>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"These may be more effective than strictly automated techniques. This is especially the case with weaknesses that are related to design and business rules." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/78894>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"This is not a perfect solution, since 100% accuracy and coverage are not feasible." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/79794>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"With Stored XSS, the indirection caused by the data store can make it more difficult to find the problem. The tester must first inject the XSS string into the data store, then find the appropriate application functionality in which the XSS string is sent to other users of the application. These are two distinct steps in which the activation of the XSS can take place minutes, hours, or days after the XSS was originally injected into the data store." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/798577>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"These may be more effective than strictly automated techniques. This is especially the case with weaknesses that are related to design and business rules." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/805626>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Without visibility into the code, black box methods may not be able to sufficiently distinguish this weakness from others, requiring manual methods to diagnose the underlying problem." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/805860>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"Detection techniques for buffer-related errors are more mature than for most other weakness types." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/807578>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"The effectiveness and speed of manual analysis will be reduced if the there is not a centralized security mechanism, and the security logic is widely distributed throughout the software." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/862742>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"These may be more effective than strictly automated techniques. This is especially the case with weaknesses that are related to design and business rules. However, manual efforts might not achieve desired code coverage within limited time constraints." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/863742>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"These may be more effective than strictly automated techniques. This is especially the case with weaknesses that are related to design and business rules. However, manual efforts might not achieve desired code coverage within limited time constraints." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/detectionMethod/89902>	ns2:detectionEffectivenessNote	"This is not a perfect solution, since 100% accuracy and coverage are not feasible." .
