<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/599172>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"OMISSION: This weakness is caused by missing a security tactic during the architecture and design phase." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/601172>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"OMISSION: This weakness is caused by missing a security tactic during the architecture and design phase." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/602168>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"COMMISSION: This weakness refers to an incorrect design related to an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/602493>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"Consider a product that consists of two or more processes or nodes that must interact closely, such as a client/server model. If the product uses protection schemes in the client in order to defend from attacks against the server, and the server does not use the same schemes, then an attacker could modify the client in a way that bypasses those schemes. This is a fundamental design flaw that is primary to many weaknesses." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/603168>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"COMMISSION: This weakness refers to an incorrect design related to an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/610168>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"COMMISSION: This weakness refers to an incorrect design related to an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/611154>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"REALIZATION: This weakness is caused during implementation of an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/61131>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"These are typically reported for temporary files or privileged programs." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/613154>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"REALIZATION: This weakness is caused during implementation of an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/6168>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"COMMISSION: This weakness refers to an incorrect design related to an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/619220>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"This issue is currently reported for unhandled exceptions, but it is theoretically possible any time the programmer does not close the cursor at the proper time." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/620154>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"REALIZATION: This weakness is caused during implementation of an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/625192>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"This problem is frequently found when the regular expression is used in input validation or security features such as authentication." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/639163>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"REALIZATION: This weakness is caused during implementation of an architectural security tactic." .
<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/640168>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"COMMISSION: This weakness refers to an incorrect design related to an architectural security tactic." .
