<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/cwe/modeOfIntroduction/783375>	ns2:modeOfIntroductionNote	"Logic errors related to operator precedence may cause problems even during normal operation, so they are probably discovered quickly during the testing phase. If testing is incomplete or there is a strong reliance on manual review of the code, then these errors may not be discovered before the software is deployed." .
